# Polaris — Startup Incubation Management Platform
# RNS Institute of Technology, Bengaluru | Team Polaris | 2025
# Cursor rules for vibe coding — read this before writing ANY code.

## WHAT THIS PROJECT IS
Full-stack web app for managing startup incubation programs.
Five roles: admin, founder, mentor, investor, manager.
Stack: Next.js 14 + Supabase + Vercel. That's it. No custom server. Ever.

---

## TECH STACK — USE ONLY THESE, NEVER SUGGEST ALTERNATIVES

| What           | Use This              | Never Use              |
|----------------|-----------------------|------------------------|
| Framework      | Next.js 14 App Router | Pages Router, Express  |
| Language       | TypeScript strict      | JavaScript, `any`      |
| Styling        | Tailwind CSS           | CSS modules, styled-components |
| UI Components  | shadcn/ui only         | Radix directly, MUI, Chakra |
| State          | Zustand                | Redux, Context API for global state |
| Server state   | TanStack React Query v5| SWR, useEffect fetching |
| Forms          | React Hook Form + Zod  | Formik, uncontrolled inputs |
| Charts         | Recharts only          | Chart.js, Victory, ApexCharts |
| Auth           | Supabase Auth          | NextAuth, Clerk, Auth.js |
| Database       | Supabase PostgreSQL     | Prisma, Drizzle, raw SQL client |
| Access control | Supabase RLS           | middleware-only auth   |
| File storage   | Supabase Storage        | S3, Cloudinary         |
| Background jobs| Supabase Edge Functions (Deno) | Node.js scripts, cron servers |
| Deployment     | Vercel                 | Docker, Kubernetes, Railway |

---

## ARCHITECTURE — TWO TIERS ONLY

```
Browser
  └── Next.js (App Router) — TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui
        ├── Middleware — auth session check + role-based route protection
        └── Supabase JS Client
              ├── PostgreSQL (auto-generated REST)
              ├── Auth (sessions, OAuth, user_metadata.role)
              ├── Realtime (dashboard live updates)
              ├── Storage (pitch decks, documents)
              └── Edge Functions (Deno — emails, aggregates)
```

**There is NO custom Express/Node server. Zero. Never add one.**
If logic can't run on the frontend → it goes in a Supabase Edge Function.

---

## ENV VARIABLES

```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=   # server-side / Edge Functions only — NEVER expose to browser
```

---

## USER ROLES

Stored in `user_metadata.role` in Supabase Auth.
Enforced at TWO layers: Next.js middleware (routing) + Supabase RLS (data).

| Role      | What they do                                               |
|-----------|------------------------------------------------------------|
| admin     | Full control — cohorts, mentor assignment, app review      |
| founder   | Own startup only — application, milestones, funding        |
| mentor    | Assigned startups only — sessions, feedback                |
| investor  | Read-only — startup progress, funding milestones           |
| manager   | Programs, events, workshops, cohort logistics              |

**RLS is the real security boundary. Frontend route guards are just UX.**

---

## DATABASE SCHEMA

```
users               — id, email
startups            — id, founder_id, name, sector, stage, status,
                      strategy_summary, target_market, revenue_model,
                      competitive_advantage, strategy_updated_at
applications        — id, startup_id, program_id, status, submitted_at
programs            — id, name, cohort, start_date, end_date, manager_id,
                      cohort_start, cohort_end, demo_day_date, max_startups
mentors             — id, user_id, expertise, bio
mentor_assignments  — mentor_id, startup_id, assigned_by, assigned_at
sessions            — id, mentor_id, startup_id, scheduled_at, notes,
                      feedback, status, rating, action_items, linked_milestone_id
milestones          — id, startup_id, title, due_date, status, completed_at
funding             — id, startup_id, type, amount, source, date, status
events              — id, program_id, title, type, date, location
event_registrations — event_id, user_id
reports             — id, startup_id, generated_by, period, data,
                      milestone_completion_rate, funding_received_cumulative,
                      session_count_period, period_start, period_end
investor_interests  — id, investor_id, startup_id, signal_type, note, created_at
application_scores  — id, application_id, reviewer_id, team_score, market_score,
                      traction_score, uniqueness_score, overall_comment, scored_at
admin_settings      — key, value, description, updated_by, updated_at
```

All PKs are `uuid`. All tables have RLS enabled. Run `supabase gen types typescript` after any schema change.

