## FILE STRUCTURE

```
/app
  /(auth)/login, /register
  /(dashboard)
    /admin/...
    /founder/...
    /mentor/...
    /investor/...
    /manager/...
  /api/   ← ONLY for 3rd-party webhooks (e.g. email provider callbacks)
/components
  /ui/          ← shadcn/ui generated — NEVER edit directly
  /shared/      ← reusable across roles
  /[module]/    ← scoped to one module (funding, events, etc.)
/lib
  /supabase/
    browser.ts  ← createBrowserClient (Client Components only)
    server.ts   ← createServerClient (Server Components + Actions)
    middleware.ts
  /validations/ ← all Zod schemas, one file per domain
  /hooks/       ← React Query hooks + Zustand stores
  /utils/
/types/         ← shared TypeScript interfaces (non-generated)
middleware.ts   ← Next.js root middleware
```

---

## PATTERNS — ALWAYS USE THESE EXACT PATTERNS

### Supabase clients — two separate files, never mix them

```ts
// lib/supabase/browser.ts — Client Components ONLY
import { createBrowserClient } from '@supabase/ssr'
export const supabase = createBrowserClient<Database>(
  process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL!,
  process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY!
)

// lib/supabase/server.ts — Server Components, Route Handlers, Actions ONLY
import { createServerClient } from '@supabase/ssr'
import { cookies } from 'next/headers'
export function createClient() {
  const cookieStore = cookies()
  return createServerClient<Database>(
    process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL!,
    process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY!,
    {
      cookies: {
        getAll: () => cookieStore.getAll(),
        setAll: (c) => c.forEach(({ name, value, options }) =>
          cookieStore.set(name, value, options))
      }
    }
  )
}
```

### Auth check — ALWAYS getUser(), NEVER getSession() server-side

```ts
// CORRECT — verifies with Supabase server
const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser()

// WRONG — reads from local storage only, never trust for authorization
const { data: { session } } = await supabase.auth.getSession()
```

### Data fetching — always through React Query hooks, never directly in components

```ts
// lib/hooks/use-milestones.ts
export function useMilestones(startupId: string) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ['milestones', startupId],
    queryFn: async () => {
      const { data, error } = await supabase
        .from('milestones')
        .select('id, title, due_date, status, completed_at')  // never use *
        .eq('startup_id', startupId)
        .order('due_date', { ascending: true })
      if (error) throw error
      return data
    },
    staleTime: 30_000,
  })
}
```

### Mutations — always invalidate query keys on success

```ts
const { mutate } = useMutation({
  mutationFn: async (data: MilestoneFormData) => {
    const { error } = await supabase.from('milestones').insert(data)
    if (error) throw error
  },
  onSuccess: () => {
    queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['milestones', startupId] })
  },
})
```

### Forms — schema first, type inferred, never written separately

```ts
// lib/validations/milestone.ts
export const milestoneSchema = z.object({
  title:    z.string().min(3),
  due_date: z.coerce.date(),
  status:   z.enum(['pending', 'in_progress', 'completed']),
})
export type MilestoneFormData = z.infer<typeof milestoneSchema>
// Use zodResolver(milestoneSchema) in useForm()
```

### Server Component page (preferred for initial data loads)

```ts
// app/(dashboard)/admin/startups/page.tsx
import { createClient } from '@/lib/supabase/server'
import { redirect } from 'next/navigation'

export default async function AdminStartupsPage() {
  const supabase = createClient()
  const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser()
  if (!user || user.user_metadata.role !== 'admin') redirect('/login')

  const { data: startups } = await supabase
    .from('startups')
    .select('id, name, sector, stage, status')
    .order('created_at', { ascending: false })

  return <StartupTable startups={startups ?? []} />
}
```

### RLS policy — always comment which role it targets

```sql
-- founders: read milestones only for startups they own
create policy "founder_select_own_milestones"
on milestones for select
using (
  startup_id in (select id from startups where founder_id = auth.uid())
);
```

### Realtime subscription — always clean up in useEffect

```ts
useEffect(() => {
  const channel = supabase
    .channel('milestones-changes')
    .on('postgres_changes',
      { event: '*', schema: 'public', table: 'milestones',
        filter: `startup_id=eq.${startupId}` },
      () => queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['milestones', startupId] })
    )
    .subscribe()
  return () => { supabase.removeChannel(channel) }
}, [startupId])
```

### Edge Function (Deno — not Node.js)

```ts
// supabase/functions/my-function/index.ts
import { serve } from 'https://deno.land/std@0.168.0/http/server.ts'
import { createClient } from 'https://esm.sh/@supabase/supabase-js@2'

serve(async (req) => {
  // Use Deno.env.get() not process.env
  // Use esm.sh for npm packages
  // No require(), no file system, must complete in 150s
  return new Response('OK')
})
```

---

## RULES — NEVER BREAK THESE

### Security
- Enable RLS on EVERY new table immediately after `create table`
- Every table needs at least one `select` and one `insert`/`update` policy
- Use `getUser()` for all server-side auth — never `getSession()`
- Never put `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` in client-side code
- Pair every frontend route guard with an RLS policy

### Database
- Never use `select('*')` in production — list columns explicitly
- All PKs are `uuid` using `gen_random_uuid()`
- When updating sessions, map fields explicitly — never spread a form data object
- To avoid funding row multiplication in aggregate views, use correlated subqueries for SUM

### TypeScript
- Strict mode — no `any`, no `as unknown as X`
- Always type Supabase results using generated `Database` types
- Derive types from Zod: `type T = z.infer<typeof schema>`

### Components
- Never edit files in `/components/ui/` — they are shadcn/ui generated
- Use Server Components for initial data loads; Client Components only when you need hooks/events/realtime
- Never call Supabase directly inside a component — always use a React Query hook
- Never use `<form>` HTML element — use React Hook Form

### Supabase-specific
- After any schema change: `supabase gen types typescript --local > types/database.ts`
- For Realtime: enable table replication in Supabase Dashboard → Database → Replication
- Edge Functions run on Deno: use `esm.sh` imports, `Deno.env.get()`, no `require()`
- For email in Edge Functions: fetch founder email via `auth.admin.getUserById()` using the service role key — the `applications` table does not store email

